course: dictionary
lesson: 1197
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Bubble is a good example. In «Bubbles start at tiny places like scratches or specks», the words scratches, specks and glasses show you that a bubble is a little ball of gas inside a drink.
explain: The same word can be a thing or a doing word. In «Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak (fried leftover cabbage and potato)», the brackets tell you what the name means. When you meet a new meaning, try it in the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: Bubble can also describe a feeling. To be bubbling with excitement means you are full of it, so a child who is bubbling with excitement is very excited. Check the clues around the word before you decide which meaning is right.
fact: A bubble is a thin round ball of liquid with air or gas inside, like a soap bubble.
fact: A bubble in a drink is a ball of gas inside a liquid, like the bubbles in fizzy drinks.
fact: To bubble means to make bubbles, like soup bubbling in a pan.
fact: To bubble with a feeling means to be full of it.
fact: Bubbles of steam rise when water boils, and a bubbling pan is hot, so be careful.
exercise: «Bubbles start at tiny places like scratches or specks.» In this sentence, what is a bubble? | A loud noise from the kitchen | A small fish in the sea | *A ball of gas inside a liquid | A thin ball of soap that you blow
exercise: «Humpback whales work together to blow a spiral net of bubbles that traps a shoal of fish.» What do the bubbles do? | *They trap fish | They turn the sea green | They melt the ice | They make the whales sing
exercise: The soup was bubbling in the pan. Find and copy the word that means making bubbles. | pan | soup | was | *bubbling
test: «They trap the gas, so the dough swells, and every hole in a slice of bread is where a bubble once was.» What does a bubble show here? | *A pocket of gas that was once in the dough | A bit of butter | A hole the baker made with a knife | A crispy crust
test: Lily is bubbling with excitement before her birthday. What does bubbling with excitement mean? | Very quiet | *Full of excitement | Boiling hot | Covered in soap
exam: «Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak.» Using the words in brackets, what is bubble-and-squeak? | A kind of soap | A bath full of foam | *A fried dish of leftover cabbage and potato | A noise made by a pan
